# OpenClaw environment template. Copy to .env and fill with real values. Every
# token, id, and secret below is a placeholder.
#
# Two files, loaded as an overlay (later wins, missing keys fall back):
#   set -a; . .env; [ -f .env.mirror ] && . .env.mirror; set +a
#
#   * .env         Base / production. infrastructure/deploy/deploy.sh ships this
#                  to the prod host as ~/.env; boot.sh loads it and the compose
#                  files substitute ${VAR}. DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN here is the real
#                  OpenClaw (production) bot. Gitignored.
#   * .env.mirror  Mirror overlay for the local DinD test rig
#                  (scripts/prod-mirror.sh). Overrides DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN with the
#                  OpenClawMirror bot and adds the mirror-only values below.
#                  Gitignored AND never deployed, so the mirror bot token can
#                  never reach prod and the prod token never sits in a mirror
#                  file. Everything it does not set is inherited from .env.
#
# Operator tooling (deploy scripts, the mirror rig, e2e tests) reads most values
# from its own shell environment, so export them first (the `set -a; . .env ...`
# line above) rather than relying on a bare `source`.

# --- Base: router + per-channel Docker deployment (.env, installed as ~/.env on prod) ---

# Discord bot token the router runs as. In .env this is the production OpenClaw
# bot; the mirror overlay replaces it with OpenClawMirror. Raw token only (no
# "DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=" prefix inside the value).
DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=your_openclaw_bot_token_here

# Whitelist for /channel register|unregister: the auth guild and the role within
# it that grants access. Unset => /channel management fails closed.
OPENCLAW_AUTH_GUILD_ID=000000000000000000
OPENCLAW_WHITELIST_ROLE_ID=000000000000000000

# Optional higher-privilege admin role within the same auth guild: may register
# any channel (incl. on another user's behalf) and unregister any channel. Unset
# => nobody is admin (only owner/whitelisted-DM rules apply). Fails closed.
OPENCLAW_ADMIN_ROLE_ID=000000000000000000

# Host provisioning daemon the router calls over loopback for /channel
# register|unregister. Unset => those commands are disabled.
OPENCLAW_PROVISIONER_PORT=18810
OPENCLAW_PROVISIONER_TOKEN=generate_a_random_secret_here

# Agent bridge the per-channel boxes run on. boot.sh REQUIRES all three (no
# defaults): a missing value aborts the deploy rather than guessing a subnet that
# might collide on the host. The router binds its model/container proxies to the
# gateway IP so boxes reach them over the bridge while the proxies stay off the
# public NIC. Pick a subnet that is free on the host.
OPENCLAW_AGENT_NETWORK=oc-agents
OPENCLAW_AGENT_SUBNET=172.30.0.0/24
OPENCLAW_AGENT_GATEWAY=172.30.0.1

# When a non-owner messages a registered channel, reply with a Log embed
# explaining the channel belongs to someone else (default: enabled). Set to a
# falsy value (0/false/no/off) to deny silently with no reply.
OPENCLAW_ROUTER_UNAUTHORIZED_NOTICE=true

# Loopback port for the local whisper speech-to-text server used to transcribe
# voice messages. One value drives both the server bind and the router client, so
# they never drift. Unset => boot.sh defaults to 18700 (DEFAULT_WHISPER_PORT in
# src/config/port-defaults.ts). Override only if 18700 collides on the host.
# WHISPER_PORT=18700

# SSH host or alias the deploy/status scripts connect to. Read from the process
# environment, so export it before running infrastructure/deploy/deploy.sh or
# status.sh. Not needed by the prod runtime itself.
# OPENCLAW_DEPLOY_HOST=user@gateway-host

# --- Mirror overlay: put these in .env.mirror (gitignored, never deployed) ---

# The OpenClawMirror bot token. Overrides the base DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN so the mirror
# rig's router connects to Discord as a dedicated bot, never the prod one (reusing
# the prod bot would open a second gateway session and fight prod). Required for
# `scripts/prod-mirror.sh up --live`.
# DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=your_openclawmirror_bot_token_here

# The OpenClawTester bot, a mock user that drives the Discord e2e tests
# (src/discord/e2e): it posts /channel register and chats to simulate a human.
# OPENCLAW_MOCK_USER_BOT_TOKEN=your_mock_user_bot_token_here

# The mock-user bot's own user id. The router treats it as a trusted bot allowed
# to hold normal conversations with the agent (every other bot stays filtered to
# avoid reply loops). Read at runtime, so it is a mirror/test value: leave it
# unset on prod.
# OPENCLAW_MOCK_USER_BOT_ID=000000000000000000

# Comma-separated user/bot ids the router treats as admin + whitelist WITHOUT the
# auth-guild role lookup, for rigs whose router bot is not in the auth server
# (horsenuggets + the mock user). The router reads it in any environment, so leave
# it UNSET on prod (it bypasses the auth server). Unset => no override.
# OPENCLAW_ADMIN_OVERRIDE_IDS=000000000000000000,000000000000000000

# Discord user id of the human who sends the voice message in the manual voice
# transcription e2e test (voice-transcription.e2e.test.ts). The router routes a
# guild message only for the channel's recorded owner, so that test registers the
# channel on this human's behalf. Unset => that test cannot pass.
# OPENCLAW_E2E_VOICE_OWNER_ID=000000000000000000

# Host port mapped to the mirror box's sshd. Unset => scripts/prod-mirror.sh
# defaults to 2299. Override only if 2299 collides on the host.
# OPENCLAW_MIRROR_SSH_PORT=2299

# Silence the proactive heartbeat so a gateway never makes periodic (~30 min)
# background model calls. Runtime gate read by the gateway/agent process it is set
# on (still runtime-togglable via the gateway), so it takes effect wherever that
# process inherits it — e.g. a local or isolated test gateway started with
# `OPENCLAW_SKIP_HEARTBEATS=1 openclaw gateway ...`. Heartbeats run by default;
# leave unset on prod so the agent stays proactive there. (Note: the mirror rig's
# per-channel agent containers use a fixed env allowlist in agent.yml, so putting
# this in .env.mirror does not yet reach them — wiring that passthrough is a
# follow-up.)
# OPENCLAW_SKIP_HEARTBEATS=1
